Technical details: The implementation of the Random(20~50)% when crafting a new item is such that there is a 75% chance of 20% to 40%, while the remaining 25% of the time you'll get 50%, with an upper limit of 100% after including crafting bonus.

Note: [[:Category:Research|Research]], [[:Category:Trophy|Trophy]], and some [[:Category:Mount|Mount]] items are not crafted nor upgraded using crafting dusts. Research items are gained and upgraded by completing the [[Trial of Innovation]]. Trophy items are gained and upgraded through [[Expeditions]]. See [[:Category:Mount|Mounts]] for specific conditions of obtaining individual Mounts.

===Rune Progress (General)===
Any action that spends [[Crafting Dust]], such as crafting items or performing experiments, gradually fills the progress bar at the bottom of the Crafting screen. When the bar is filled, it will reset while rewarding a free [[File:TrialKey.png|x32px]] [[Rune]] - allowing you to continuously refill the bar and earn free Runes as you keep spending Crafting Dust.

The Crafting Dust cost of each action performed contributes to the progress bar as follows:

<math>P = C \times 0.045 \div 1200,</math>

where
* <math>P</math> is the progress you will earn
* <math>C</math> is the [[Crafting Dust]] cost of said action

==Experiments & Enchanting==
===Enchanting===
<div><small>''See also: [[Enchantments]]''</small></div>
After unlocking [[Paragon]] level 17 ''(1e200 [[Mysteries]])'', Legendary and Unique items can be Enchanted, to give them an additional bonus. Initially, each item can be enchanted up to 20 times, but this limit can be increased increased 25 levels by use of [[Realm Upgrades#Heritage|Heritage]] upgrades, and a further 10 levels by [[Realm Upgrades#Paramnesics|Paramnesics]] upgrades, giving a maximum enchant level of 55. Enchantment level bonuses stack multiplicatively.

[[File:Powder v2 ench.png|x32px]] Enchanting Dust is earned passively over time, at a base rate of ~836.35 Enchanting dust per 24 hours (one every 1 minute, 43 seconds). Its collection rate is not affected by [[Crafting Dust]] collection modifiers, but has its own modifiers that increase it. Enchanting Dust can also be earned from [[Trials]], investing in Experiments (see below), or as a rare drop from [[Collectibles|Bats]].

Item Enchantments start at level 0, and initially cost 100 Enchanting dust to level up, increased by 50% per level.

There are certain effects which can give 'Bonus Enchantment Levels', which give a number of free levels (up to 5) to all Enchantments on all items equipped. (However, in order for these bonus levels to be applied, the items must have at least 1 level of Enchantment.)

If you have an enchanted item you don't want anymore, you can spend a [[Nullifier Core]] (That you can buy in the [[Market]], occasionally obtain after a [[Trials|Trial ]] or from a Nullifiers [[Items#Experiments|Experiment]]) to get back all the enchanting dust spent on the item, while losing all the enchant levels on it.

You can also disenchant all of your items at once by spending 10 [[Nullifier Core|Nullifier Cores]].

All Enchanting Dust, both spent and stockpiled, is lost upon changing [[Realm]]s. However, the lost Enchanting Dust is converted into [[Memories]].

===Experiments===
Also at [[Paragon]] level 17, '''Experiments''' are unlocked. Experiments are a way to spend Crafting Dusts, once all items in the game have been crafted. Experiments are primarily a source of Enchanting Dust, however there are several other useful resources or rewards they can give.

